{
  "_comment": [
    "Living Brain's own: the provider cards on Settings -> Models and the curated model lists behind them.",
    "Hand-maintained; scripts/sync-providers never touches this file. The server compiles it in",
    "(crates/livingbrain-models/src/curated.rs) so the curated fallback a discover answers is this list.",
    "`provider` is a providers.json id (or `custom`); a `runner` card has none: it runs on the member's own",
    "device through their own CLI and subscription, and nothing about it reaches the server but the choice.",
    "`listing`: `native` = GET {base}/v1/models, an https URL = that OpenAI-compatible list (signed like the",
    "provider's own calls), `none` = the provider publishes no list, so the curated models are the answer.",
    "Model ids, context windows and prices were checked against each provider's own docs on 2026-10-15",
    "(`models_source`); a price is per million input / output tokens, and omitted where the docs gave none.",
    "Logos are self-hosted under assets/logos/ and drawn in currentColor; `logo_source` names each one.",
    "`stream` (optional, default true): `false` sends this provider's model calls unstreamed (no `\"stream\": true`).",
    "`structured` (optional): `tool` = a job that wants a structured answer (the coding-agents edit list) is sent as one",
    "forced tool call held to the answer's JSON Schema (`tools` + `tool_choice` on the card's wire); absent = plain text,",
    "parsed. Set only where it was verified against the provider (Z.AI glm-5.2 and glm-5.3-flash on 2026-10-15).",
    "`classifier` (the Jev card) is not a model for a job slot: it is the coding-agents compiler's optional triage",
    "classifier, TypeSafe's Jev. Its state is GET /v1/models/jev; `detail` is the sheet's full sentence; the model is the",
    "one cratefield-adapter-typesafe pins (`DEFAULT_MODEL`)."
  ],
